summary:
- topic: New Board Norms and Guidelines
  text: The Board Chair introduced a new set of communication norms and guidelines
    developed over the summer. These rules are intended to foster more effective and
    respectful collaboration among board members, with the administration, and the
    public.
- topic: Start of School Year Updates
  text: The student representative and superintendent provided comprehensive reports
    on the successful start of the school year. They highlighted high energy from
    students and staff, new safety vestibules at elementary schools, and positive
    feedback on the PBIS behavior program at the high school.
- topic: Nutrition Program Initiatives
  text: A detailed update on the nutrition department highlighted that all student
    meals are free, new interim leadership is in place, and several grants are funding
    initiatives for locally sourced fish, culturally relevant greens, and a program
    to provide third-party certified halal meals.
- topic: FY26 Budget and Financial Concerns
  text: The administration addressed the current budget status, acknowledging recent
    payroll errors and a potential deficit from the previous fiscal year. An external
    audit is scheduled to begin, and the district is proactively reviewing spending
    and overtime to ensure fiscal stability.
- topic: Concussion Management Policy
  text: The board discussed proposed changes to Policy JJIF regarding student concussions.
    The discussion focused on ensuring parents are notified and included in the decision-making
    process for a student's return to play, leading the board to vote to send the
    policy back to committee for further refinement.
- topic: Community and Safety Concerns
  text: Board members raised several community issues, including reminding drivers
    about school bus safety, the ongoing need for crossing guards, and the emotional
    weight of school shootings on students and staff, prompting a call to revisit
    district security practices.
- topic: Executive Sessions
  text: The board voted to add an executive session to the agenda to discuss confidential
    labor negotiations with the South Portland Teachers Association. At the end of
    the public meeting, the board entered a separate executive session to discuss
    a personnel matter.
